cookbook/decisions/recipe-choices-align-to-isaiah-without-owner-escalation.md:33:2. **Critic and value distillation.** Upstream `scaling_6m` uses the default softmax winner-distribution critic (value 2p−1, MSE value loss, gamma 1) with a last-best teacher (policy KL 0.005, winner-probability value distillation 0.005). Upstream itself rejects `critic_mode='independent'` with value distillation, so alignment means implementing winner-distribution semantics rather than relaxing that guard. V3 runs one forward per seat-private observation; a critic that combines both seats' private inputs is neither Isaiah's architecture nor required. The nearest analog follows Isaiah's stateless critic: per-player critic value tokens (self and opponent) inside each seat's own observation feed a shared head, giving one logit per player, a softmax and value 2p − 1 (plan Task 3.1). That admits upstream's value distillation without reading the rival's private state. The range check is settled by source: `terminal_scale = 1 - caps` keeps shaped returns in [-1, 1].
cookbook/decisions/preserve-the-ppo-recipe-across-bc-bootstrap.md:20:That historical recipe also used economic coefficient.2 (starvation/drought4/1, cap.25, ineffective0, terminal W/L/D scale.75; still the current shaping), 128 complete raw-bank selection games and a checkpoint interval of100,000 global game steps (now 20M, as upstream). Separate current/best checkpoints and the original 70% promotion logic remain current. The retained GPU pod stays running after bounded work unless the owner changes that instruction.
cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:33:- `python/owl/game.py` defines explicit game batch/mask/environment unions and a factory. `python/owl/rl.py` adds supported config unions and rejects mismatched families, non-two-player Kaggriculture and Orbit-only reward modes.
cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:39:- `.gitignore` excludes run output, weights, traces and credentials. `pyproject.toml` moves `kaggle`/`kaggle-environments` into an optional `reference` extra with `kaggle-environments==1.32.7`; `justfile` test recipes request that extra. Orbit reference fixtures on this host were regenerated with 1.32.7. Native-build cache keys include `engine_rs/src/**/*.rs` and `engine_rs/Cargo.toml`, so vendored engine edits rebuild the extension.
cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:44:- Kaggriculture evaluation decides W/L/D from final native banks. Summed shaped reward cannot pick the winner: an allowed .8 economic cap could otherwise score the real bank winner `.2-.8=-.6`.
cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:45:- Artificial truncation keeps the real economic reward earned on that transition and adds the critic bootstrap; Orbit keeps upstream's `rewards=0`.
cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:68:Reuse the starter's PPO machinery, DDP, scheduling, optimizer grouping and telemetry without hard-coding Orbit entity/action field names at transport boundaries. Evaluate the two-seat game with its own reward/termination definitions. Preserve behavior action densities from collection through update; changing the action representation must not silently turn joint probabilities into per-slot clipping.
cookbook/references/index.md:19:- [[reward-reuse-preserves-objective-and-critic-semantics|Reward reuse preserves objective and critic semantics]] — Current GPU econ coefficient0.2, observed nonzero reward with no claimed learning benefit, and exact v2 W/L/D, bank-margin and capped-economic formulas with v3 critic/bootstrap compatibility limits.
cookbook/references/index.md:23:- [[kaggriculture-grammar-heads-sit-behind-isaiahs-actor-projection|Kaggriculture grammar heads sit behind Isaiah's actor projection]] — Task 2.3 adds the 3D→D actor projection and batched grammar heads with exact coupled-Gumbel HIRE sampling, same-path replay with support/length/canonical flags and one host check, head GEMM-extent chunking, and a 6,252,223-parameter preset; synthetic grammar tables stand in until Task 1.2. Describes the current tree.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:17:Both-zero terminal W/L/D gives no ranking signal between these policies. Econ.2 is a capped death-potential difference, not a penalty for arbitrary spending or a bank-profit target. The current-policy diagnostic also accumulates8193 ineffective unit commands; economic production chains remain unlearned. Prior cookbook search found no qualified v3 BC implementation; v2's public replay loader provides observation/action alignment and shared-field semantics, not its model, collector or training code.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:23:- `ops/bc-bootstrap-2026-09-29/select_replays.py`, `prepare.py`: read-only source volume4llk4uaf20, source days09-21..27, seeded32 training and4 validation episodes/day.252 episodes are split by identity, with duplicate episode basenames rejected in preparation. Hash each source payload and prepared shard. Pair observation[t] with action[t+1], fill seat1 schema-shared fields, and preserve own-private encoding. Omitted units are filled with Python `None`, which `actor_codec._unit_frame` rejects; the earlier claim that they become explicit NONE was incorrect. Never truncate market orders or quantities. Replay JSON is processed once offline; resident GPU arrays feed BC minibatches. The [[rebuild-data-preparation-preserves-replay-identity|rebuild Reference]] records the source check and v4 admission consequence; this correction does not alter the historical manifest counts.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:31:Eager two-rank smoke passes8 updates/4096 seat turns with validation NLL3.648→3.575 on two episodes. Full-data compiled two-rank smoke passes8 updates/4096 seat turns with NLL3.925→3.853. Independent checks confirm finite updated actor weights, unchanged critic-head tensors and canonical checkpoint key compatibility. Cold smoke throughput is not a sustained BC benchmark. The original smoke checkpoint metadata included BC-only keys; the harness was corrected and rerun before launch so weights-only handoff uses the canonical schema, with BC metadata in separate artifacts.
