   533	
   534	Isaiah gives the borrowing style, not batch atomicity: W:src/rl/vec_env.rs:214,229,292 validates/slices buffers; :1561 mutates live states with global Rayon; :1674 collects errors. W:src/rl.rs:139 maps shape errors. Its env does not release the GIL. Rebuild with PyO3 0.28 `py.detach`, holding all NumPy borrow guards for the **entire** operation. Detached closures capture only owned candidates/Send validated slices, not Python objects. A caller may not access borrowed arrays concurrently; NumPy's borrow guards do not protect CUDA DMA, hence Python fences.
