   749	- **L6 trainer path.** `ppo.py` enables nonblocking copies only for CUDA + pinned (:561–563). The rollout loop enqueues reward/done copies (:882–889) and the next-observation copy (:912–916) on the current stream. The next `env.step` follows a forward and a blocking `.to("cpu")` of the actions (:2273–2281, :2301). Truncation indexes `next_obs` into an unpinned copy before `truncate_envs` (:975–991). A repository grep for `cuda.Stream`, `torch.cuda.stream`, `Event(`, `wait_stream` and `record_stream` finds no side streams. Eval copies are nonblocking on CUDA (run_ppo.py:1582–1590).
   750	- **Isaiah's env** (`src/rl/vec_env.rs`) borrows `PyReadwriteArrayDyn` buffers, uses the global rayon pool, does not release the GIL, and truncates in place (:540–547). PyO3 is 0.28.3 in `Cargo.lock`.
   751	- **Kernel facts.** Termination is horizon-only: `previous_step >= episodeSteps − 2` (`engine_rs/src/lib.rs:1487`), so the default game ends at transition 719, and `episodeSteps` 1 and 2 end after one transition. `step_with_market_metrics` already clones and commits only on success (:1431–1449), so the baseline really is two clones plus one snapshot. `econ_counters()` is public (:1370) and S/D/I are indices 0/1/2 (:1120–1122).
