   193	## Adapter behavior and the L6 fence
   194	
   195	`allocate_observation_buffers` writes the29 shapes/dtypes in the copied inventory and constructs **existing** `KaggricultureObsBatch` and `KaggricultureActionMask`. Build exact named NumPy views once in an internal typed `NativeArrays` holder; it mirrors binding parameters, not another policy schema. All tensor storage retained. No `.numpy()`/shape inference/reward recalculation per step; no returned NumPy allocations. Allocate the six transition tensors once and pass all 35 keywords explicitly to1.4. Fail requested pinning if allocator unavailable; CPU tests pass pin_memory=False. Orbit behavior is unchanged.
   196	
   197	The adapter owns one buffer set: the observation batch, the six transition tensors and their native views. The constructor fills it via native `observe`. `reset`/`step`/`truncate_envs` each run the entry fence, then the native call; on failure the native side has published nothing, so every byte is unchanged; on success they return the same (identity-stable) batch, as Isaiah's `VectorizedEnv` does. `terminal_metrics` delegates lazily; snapshot JSON/seed tuple are diagnostics only. Do not expose a lifecycle explicit-state loader.
   198	
   199	Action input accepts only KaggricultureActions with exact int64 CPU tensors, `[E,2,252,12]`/`[E,2]`, C-contiguous; rejects GPU/dtype/shape/strides instead of silently casting/copying. Task 3.1 owns device→CPU action transfer and contiguous materialization. Native checks every grammar constraint. Truncate mask must be exact bool CPU `[E]`; no `.cpu()` surprise synchronization in adapter.
   200	
   201	Fence contract (R1, shared ABI above): `_fence()` runs first in every mutating method. It calls `torch.cuda.current_stream(self.transfer_device).synchronize()` iff `transfer_device.type == "cuda"` and the buffers are pinned; otherwise it makes no CUDA call. The callable is injected only in tests (a spy), never via a public switch. It waits for every device read enqueued before the env call; readers on other streams must join the current stream first (none exist today).
   202	
   203	The fence needs no trainer call. Its real-DMA proof is the pod test in Task C, not the Mac spy test. No claim of fixing the historical Task 0.2 GEMM overflow.
