   812	
   813	- **R1 — seeded-game coverage** (Corpus section). The drafted eight-command policy never builds, buys animals, feeds, cares, fertilizes, digs or moves goods. Seeded mid/late states would therefore contain no structures, animals or fertilizer, and animals would appear only in synthetic states. The policy now cycles all 18 unit kinds and all market kinds with rotating items. The manifest must meet explicit coverage quotas on non-synthetic records, and generation fails rather than lowering a quota.
   814	- **R2 — decides Q1: strict tile shapes.** Tile objects must match engine-produced key sets. Stale inapplicable keys, `"animal": null` and unknown keys are rejected, not ignored. Integer fields, including `pending_care_bonus`, must be JSON integers. The engine never produces stale keys: animal death rewrites the tile to `{"kind": structure}` at `lib.rs:4287`, and the bonus is `map_i64`. So this loses no legal state, and it makes every admitted state legacy-reconstructible. Task D gained the matching rejection tests, and the 1027–3826 row no longer carries the fractional-bonus caveat. No contract change is needed.
   815	- **R3 — fixture budget.** Lowered from 16 MiB to ≤ 8 MiB compressed; the committed official traces total about 1 MiB, and CLAUDE.md keeps bulk corpora out of git. The only allowed lossless remedy is a deterministic byte-plane shuffle, documented in the manifest. Otherwise stop and ask.
   816	- **R4 — timing evidence.** Debug-profile timings may not drive the snapshot-path reopening decision. The timing runs in an optimized build, and its (fat-LTO) build time is recorded. If the build exceeds the Mac bound, the same command runs on the pod instead.
